From 2262eddeebeb2264192ceff125fde84cb6c96540 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BreDoyliesSea <doylies@encrypt.eu>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:11:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 57/58] cpu: End a guest function that is executing in the
 first page (#4290)

* cpu: End a guest function that is executing in the first page

A thread whose PC is in the first page has jumped through a null or wiped
pointer. Every instruction fetch there was an invalid read that returned
0, which decodes as a plain instruction, so the JIT went on translating
one block through unmapped memory, logging each fetch, until the
emulator was closed.

A fetch from the first page now fails, so the block ends in a no-execute
fault, and the fault ends the thread's guest function the way
WaitForInterrupt does: the thread returns instead of spinning there.
Suggested in review of #4198.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* cpu: Check the Vita's first page and log the stopped thread's state

The first page is the Vita's 4 KiB one, not the host's, which can be
larger. The stop now logs the thread's registers too, as the invalid
read and write reports do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* ci: Expect gxm_shader_patcher_memory to fail instead of timing out

Its NULL host alloc callback still jumps to 0, but the thread is now
stopped there, so the test finishes and fails on the patcher regions and
error codes instead of timing out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* ci: Keep gxm_shader_patcher_memory's reason as it was

Only its expected result changes, from timeout to fail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* Change gxm_shader_patcher_memory status to timeout

---------

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-authored-by: Pedro Montes Alcalde <pedro.montes.alcalde@gmail.com>
